To check images present locally - docker images
To check all the running containers - docker ps
To pull any image from repository to local -  docker pull imageName
We don't need to docker pull separately. docker run automatically pulls the image and starts container if it's not already on our machine - docker run postgres:16
Can run same application of multiple versions without any conflict.
Sequence-
      docker pull redis
      docker run redis
      docker run -d redis
Restart a container(maybe crashed or something like that)-
 
docker stop 8453671ndg43(id of the container)

If we again start the container -

docker start 789y67894rr(id of the container)

To check container history(If we open laptop the next day and can’t find anything)- 

      docker ps -a (lists running and stopped container)
 
We will get the lists with container ids and then we can restart it again with the help of the ids. 

Suppose we want to run same application with diff versions in same time/diff time. Ex: Redis 
 
 docker run redis:4.0

There are two types of ports - container port and machine port. In order to run the application,they must be binded.
Now containers can have same port number,but machine port can’t be same. Below are the commands to bind same application of diff versions,having same container port numbers to host port.





docker run -p6000:6379 redis


Where p=port
6000=machine port no
6379=container port no


